---
import { Callout, Code, CodeTabs, Link } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'

const brewInstall = 'brew install santi020k/tap/santi020k-terminal && santi020k-terminal configure'
const scriptInstall = 'curl --proto \'=https\' --tlsv1.2 -fsSL https://theme.santi020k.com/terminal/zsh/install.zsh | zsh'

const installOptions = [
  { value: 'homebrew', label: 'Homebrew (recommended)', code: brewInstall, language: 'sh' },
  { value: 'script', label: 'Hosted installer', code: scriptInstall, language: 'sh' }
]

const headings = [{ id: 'choose-setup', label: 'Choose your setup' }, { id: 'requirements', label: 'Requirements' }, { id: 'install', label: 'Install' }, { id: 'verify', label: 'Verify setup' }, { id: 'script', label: 'Inspect the installer' }, { id: 'next-steps', label: 'Next steps' }]
---
<DocsLayout title="Getting started" description="Set up your shell and prompt on macOS, or download just the colors for your terminal." path="/terminal/docs/" {headings}>
  <section id="choose-setup">
    <h2>Choose your setup</h2>
    <p>Keep your existing shell configuration if all you need is the palette.</p>
    <div class="docs-link-list">
      <Link href="#requirements"><b>Complete setup on macOS →</b><span>Install the CLI, managed shell integration, and a Starship prompt with Homebrew.</span></Link>
      <Link href="/terminal/docs/terminal-colors/"><b>Terminal colors only →</b><span>Download dark or light presets for six terminal apps without installing the CLI.</span></Link>
      <Link href="/terminal/configure/"><b>Preview your choices →</b><span>Choose your shell, prompt, terminal, and palette in the guided configurator.</span></Link>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="requirements">
    <h2>Before you install</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use macOS for the Homebrew setup. Zsh is the default; see the <Link href="/terminal/docs/shells/">Bash and Fish guide</Link> for other shells.</li>
      <li>Install Homebrew and make sure <code>brew</code> is available in your shell.</li>
      <li>Use a Nerd Font if you want the Powerline prompt symbols.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section id="install">
    <h2>Install the complete setup</h2>
    <p>Choose one installation path. Homebrew installs the formula, then opens the guided configuration. The hosted installer downloads the current configuration and installs the same Homebrew dependencies.</p>
    <Callout className="docs-callout"><b>Homebrew is recommended</b><p>It owns the CLI, theme assets, shell completions, and dependencies, making updates and removal predictable.</p></Callout>
    <CodeTabs items={installOptions} ariaLabel="Terminal installation methods" codeLabel="Terminal installation command" copyLabel="Copy selected installation command" theme="santi020k" wrap={false} />
    <p>The installer backs up files it manages, writes configuration to <code>~/.config/santi020k-terminal</code>, and adds one source line to your existing <code>~/.zshrc</code>. Start a fresh session when it finishes:</p>
    <Code variant="block" code="exec zsh" language="sh" label="Restart your shell" copy copyLabel="Copy Zsh restart command" theme="santi020k" />
  </section>
  <section id="verify">
    <h2>Check your setup</h2>
    <p>After restarting your shell, inspect the managed state and check dependencies, configuration, shell integration, and Nerd Font availability.</p>
    <Code variant="block" code={'santi020k-terminal status\nsanti020k-terminal doctor'} language="sh" label="Verify terminal setup" copy copyLabel="Copy setup verification commands" theme="santi020k" />
    <p>If a check reports a problem, follow the <Link href="/terminal/docs/cli/#maintenance">health and recovery reference</Link> before reinstalling.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="script">
    <h2>Inspect the hosted installer</h2>
    <p>The hosted command executes a downloaded shell script. <Link href="/terminal/zsh/install.zsh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the installer source <span class="external-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></Link> before running it to review the managed files and dependency installation.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="next-steps">
    <h2>Make it yours</h2>
    <div class="docs-link-list">
      <Link href="/terminal/docs/zsh/"><b>Understand the Zsh setup</b><span>Plugins, tools, history, and managed configuration.</span></Link>
      <Link href="/terminal/docs/starship/"><b>Choose a prompt preset</b><span>Compare rich, portable, and minimal Starship configurations.</span></Link>
      <Link href="/terminal/docs/terminal-colors/"><b>Install terminal colors</b><span>Apply the dark or light palette to your terminal application.</span></Link>
      <Link href="/terminal/docs/cli/"><b>Learn the CLI</b><span>Switch presets, check status, update, repair, or uninstall.</span></Link>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
